IMPORT prelude

-- Environmental Public Health Act 1987 (Singapore) -- Part 9A, the general cleaning industry: who is a cleaner (s 2), the
-- licence requirement and its presumption (s 80D), engaging an unlicensed cleaning business (s 80E), the progressive wage
-- licence condition and the Commissioner for Labour's minimum basic wage order (s 80H), and the sanctions for breaking a
-- licence condition (ss 80J, 80K).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EPHA1987.txt. The
-- deposit's running footer reads "version in force from 1/7/2026" (retrieved 1 October 2026), later than the edition named
-- in encoding.json for the littering module.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0275 (Jun Hao scenario, event j088, 2056): the lowest monthly
-- basic wage a licensed cleaning business may pay a general cleaner in February 2056, and where it is written.
--
-- THE LEDGER NAMED THE WRONG SECTION. s 31AA is headed "Prescribed conditions relating to progressive wage model for waste
-- collection industry" and binds waste collector licensees; s 23A does the same for the waste disposal industry. The
-- cleaning industry's progressive wage condition is s 80H(1)(b) and (2), in Part 9A.
--
-- THE FIGURE IS NOT IN THE ACT. s 80H(2)(a): the Commissioner for Labour "must, by order, specify ... the minimum amount of
-- basic wage and the date that minimum amount takes effect". The order (and the class "general cleaner", which the Act
-- never names) is an INPUT here. The licence condition itself exists only if regulations under s 111 prescribe it
-- (s 80H(1): "conditions that may be prescribed by regulations made under section 111, which may include"); that too is an
-- input.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the progressive wage model bonus and its frequency (s 80H(2)(b)); training conditions (s 80H(1)(c),
-- s 80G(4)(d)); licence classes, eligibility and application (ss 80F, 80G); the Director-General's own conditions
-- (s 80H(8) to (11)); appeals (ss 80G(7), 80J(7), 80K(3)); changes of information, monitoring and the register (ss 80L to
-- 80N); waste management workers (ss 23A, 31AA, 31DA); the Employment Act 1968, which sets no general minimum wage and is
-- not read here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Environmental Public Health Act 1987 -- cleaning industry wages`

§§ `23A, 31AA, 80H -- which section carries the progressive wage condition`

-- s 23A heading: "Prescribed conditions relating to progressive wage model for waste disposal industry".
-- s 31AA heading: "Prescribed conditions relating to progressive wage model for waste collection industry".
-- s 80H heading: "Conditions of cleaning business licence"; (1)(b) the basic wage of "every cleaner who is a citizen or
-- permanent resident of Singapore (called in this section a resident cleaner)".
DECLARE Industry IS ONE OF
    `general cleaning`
    `waste collection`
    `waste disposal`

GIVEN `the industry` IS AN Industry
GIVETH A STRING
`the section carrying the progressive wage condition for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the industry`
    WHEN `general cleaning` THEN "80H"
    WHEN `waste collection` THEN "31AA"
    OTHERWISE "23A"

GIVETH A STRING
`where the cleaner's minimum basic wage is written` MEANS
    "an order of the Commissioner for Labour under s 80H(2)(a), applied through a licence condition prescribed by regulations under ss 80H(1)(b) and 111"

§§ `2 -- cleaner, resident cleaner`

-- s 2: "cleaner" means an individual who is engaged, "whether as a full-time employee, part-time employee or casual employee
-- and whether or not at piece rates" -- (a) "to perform cleaning work for a person other than the individual's employer"; or
-- (b) to supervise others doing so; "and includes any individual who is declared by the Minister, by notification in the
-- Gazette, to be a cleaner".
-- s 80H(1)(b): a "resident cleaner" is a cleaner "who is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore".
DECLARE Worker HAS
    `performs cleaning work for someone other than the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supervises such cleaning work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared a cleaner by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works under a cleaning contract made before the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker is a cleaner` IF
        `the worker`'s `performs cleaning work for someone other than the employer`
    OR `the worker`'s `supervises such cleaning work`
    OR `the worker`'s `declared a cleaner by the Minister`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker is a resident cleaner` IF
    `the worker is a cleaner` `the worker` AND `the worker`'s `is a citizen or permanent resident`

§§ `80D -- the licence requirement`

-- s 80D(1): "A person must not carry on a cleaning business in Singapore, except under and in accordance with a cleaning
-- business licence that is in force." (2): fine "not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12
-- months or ... both" and for a continuing offence "a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day"
-- after conviction.
-- (3): presumed, "until the contrary is proved", to carry on a cleaning business if the person charges or receives, or
-- undertakes for, a fee or reward for providing cleaning work to others, and (a) "by contract of service, the person employs
-- 2 or more individuals as cleaners"; (b) by contract (whether or not of service) "engages 2 or more individuals to perform
-- the cleaning work" (the deposit's text of (b) is garbled, with a stray "(b) the person, having -- (i) to achieve a stated
-- result ... (ii) to supply ... plant or equipment"; read here as one paragraph); or (c) "being a principal contractor"
-- engages a person within (a) or (b).
DECLARE Business HAS
    `charges a fee or reward for providing cleaning work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cleaners employed under contracts of service` IS A NUMBER
    `individuals engaged by any contract to clean` IS A NUMBER
    `is a principal contractor engaging such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a cleaning business licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is presumed to carry on a cleaning business` IF
    `the business`'s `charges a fee or reward for providing cleaning work`
    AND (    `the business`'s `cleaners employed under contracts of service` AT LEAST 2
          OR `the business`'s `individuals engaged by any contract to clean` AT LEAST 2
          OR `the business`'s `is a principal contractor engaging such a person`)

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is presumed to be in breach of section 80D` IF
    `the business is presumed to carry on a cleaning business` `the business`
    AND (NOT `the business`'s `holds a cleaning business licence in force`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 80D` MEANS 10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 80D` MEANS 12

§§ `80E -- engaging an unlicensed cleaning business`

-- s 80E(1): where A "enters into or renews any contract (other than a contract of service)" with B for cleaning work by
-- B's cleaners "on premises or any public place owned, occupied or managed by A", and B "does not hold a valid cleaning
-- business licence", then "whether or not any criminal proceedings are instituted against B", A is guilty of an offence:
-- fine not exceeding $10,000, and $1,000 a day for a continuing offence. (2): defence for A to prove "on a balance of
-- probabilities" that A "did not know and could not reasonably have been expected to know".
GIVEN `contract for cleaning A's premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `B is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN, `A could not reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `A is liable under section 80E` IF
    `contract for cleaning A's premises` AND (NOT `B is licensed`) AND (NOT `A could not reasonably have known`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 80E` MEANS 10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `80H -- the minimum basic wage`

-- s 80H(1)(b): conditions "requiring every contract of service entered into between the cleaning business licensee and every
-- cleaner who is a citizen or permanent resident ... to provide for the payment of a basic wage ... that -- (i) is not less
-- than the amount ... specified by order under subsection (2) for the class of cleaners that the resident cleaner belongs to".
-- (2)(a): the Commissioner for Labour "must, by order, specify ... the minimum amount of basic wage and the date that minimum
-- amount takes effect". (3): different amounts "for different classes of cleaners", "varied from time to time".
-- (6): the amount takes effect "even though the basic wage that would have been payable to a cleaner under any collective
-- agreement ... is lower than that amount".
-- (7): the Director-General "may, by written notice to cleaning business licensees, postpone the effective date" for
-- cleaners employed "under any cleaning contract entered into by cleaning business licensees before that effective date".
-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers and only compared.
DECLARE `Wage order` HAS
    `minimum monthly basic wage before the order` IS A NUMBER
    `minimum monthly basic wage under the order` IS A NUMBER
    `effective date` IS A NUMBER
    `postponed effective date` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the order` IS A `Wage order`, `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date the order binds for` MEANS
    IF `the order`'s `postponed effective date` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the worker`'s `works under a cleaning contract made before the effective date`
    THEN `the order`'s `postponed effective date`
    ELSE `the order`'s `effective date`

GIVEN `regulations prescribe the basic-wage condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the business` IS A Business, `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basic-wage condition binds the employer for this worker` IF
    `regulations prescribe the basic-wage condition`
    AND `the business`'s `holds a cleaning business licence in force`
    AND `the worker is a resident cleaner` `the worker`

-- Returns 0 where the Act sets no floor for this worker (not a resident cleaner, unlicensed employer, or no condition
-- prescribed). 0 means "no floor under this Act", not "may pay nothing": the Employment Act 1968 and the contract are not read.
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the basic-wage condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the business` IS A Business, `the worker` IS A Worker, `the order` IS A `Wage order`, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lowest monthly basic wage under the Act` MEANS
    IF NOT `the basic-wage condition binds the employer for this worker` `regulations prescribe the basic-wage condition` `the business` `the worker`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the date` AT LEAST `the date the order binds for` `the order` `the worker`
         THEN `the order`'s `minimum monthly basic wage under the order`
         ELSE `the order`'s `minimum monthly basic wage before the order`

-- s 80H(6): a lower collective-agreement wage does not reduce the floor. INFERENCE (not in the text): a higher
-- collective-agreement wage is owed under the agreement, so the larger of the two is what the employer may not go below.
GIVEN `the floor` IS A NUMBER, `collective agreement wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lowest basic wage allowing for a collective agreement` MEANS
    IF `collective agreement wage` GREATER THAN `the floor` THEN `collective agreement wage` ELSE `the floor`

GIVEN `wage paid` IS A NUMBER, `the floor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basic wage complies with the condition` IF `wage paid` AT LEAST `the floor`

§§ `80J, 80K -- sanctions for breaking the condition`

-- s 80J(1)(k): revocation if the licensee "has failed to comply with any condition of its cleaning business licence".
-- (2)(a): if not grave enough, suspension "for any period of time (not exceeding 6 months)". (3): an opportunity of being
-- heard "being a period of not less than 3 days but not more than 14 days". (4): for "the licence condition referred to in
-- section 80H(1)(b)", not "unless the Director-General has first consulted the Commissioner for Labour".
-- s 80K(1): a financial penalty "not exceeding $5,000", "in lieu of or in addition to" revocation or suspension; (2) the same
-- prior consultation for the s 80H(1)(b) condition.
GIVEN `consulted the Commissioner for Labour` IS A BOOLEAN, `days given to be heard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may revoke or suspend for a basic-wage breach` IF
    `consulted the Commissioner for Labour` AND `days given to be heard` AT LEAST 3 AND `days given to be heard` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `consulted the Commissioner for Labour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may impose a financial penalty for a basic-wage breach` IF
    `consulted the Commissioner for Labour`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty under section 80K` MEANS 5000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest suspension in months under section 80J` MEANS 6
